Project scope and provenance notice

The current garment example is independently authored procedural geometry: Cartesian support and cloth grids, one bone, a translation clip and code-painted geometric texture. Its explicit configuration is a geometric mechanics example, not human/garment fidelity, original-asset recreation, native acceptance, or rights evidence.

Historical asset-specific garment calibration, measured tables, body-part inventories, transfer studies and copied garment receipts have been removed/replaced in the current tree. Generic algorithms are retained. This change does not erase repository history, establish the provenance of historical inputs, grant rights to any former or caller-supplied asset, or constitute legal approval.

Real-input users must independently establish source permissions and attribution and supply their own calibration, catalogues and measured evidence. Synthetic fixtures do not relax source admission, G10, native-control, renderer, material, rigging or export-parity gates.

